{"content":"⚠️ **IMPORTANT: tautological assertion — this check can never fail**

```js
assert.ok(!result.log.some(function (l) {
    return l.indexOf('FIFO-queued') !== -1 && l.indexOf('pr-3') !== -1;
}) === false || true, 'pr-3 stays queued behind pr-2 (FIFO preserved)');
```

`(!X === false) || true` is always `true`, so the assertion verifies nothing while its message claims to pin FIFO ordering ("pr-3 stays queued behind pr-2"). As written the suite reports a guarantee it does not actually make.

Note the intended assertion is also untestable in this shape: after pr-2 consumes the vacated slot and defers as `BEHIND`, pr-3 *also* logs a `FIFO-queued` line (nothing sets `deadHeadPassed` again), so "pr-3 did not log FIFO-queued" would be RED against the current (correct) behavior. The property you actually want — pr-3 did not merge — is already covered by `assert.equal(fx.calls.merges.length, 0, ...)` above; to also pin FIFO behind a non-ready candidate, assert on merge attempts and `skipped`:

```js
assert.equal(fx.calls.merges.length, 0, 'neither pr-2 nor pr-3 merges while pr-2 is BEHIND');
assert.equal(result.skipped, 1, 'only the blocked head is skipped');
```

Either delete the tautology or replace it with a real one — a green assertion that cannot fail erodes the suite's signal (RED-before-fix claim included).
